    "prefecture": "kanagawa",
    "category": "kyodo",
    "summary": {
      "text": "Drum cakes, or kankoyaki, are a food made by packing a wheat-flower dough full of ingredients and then frying and steaming it. They are similar to oyaki dumplings. For the filling, people use local ingredients that match the season, such as edible wild vegetables, adzuki beans, pumpkin, mushrooms, and pickles.",
