      "text": "Oyama, located 1,252 meters above sea level and part of the Tanzawa Oyama National Park, is famous for its tofu, which makes use of the good quality water of the Tanzawa mountain range. Tofu is very soft with high water content and has a light flavor. Because it can be easily combined with any ingredients, a variety of tofu dishes are served in local households, but the two most popular are \"chilled tofu\" and \"yudofu,\" which allow the flavors of the ingredients to be enjoyed as they are.Because Mt.",
