      "ja": "生しらす丼",
      "kana": "なましらすどん",
      "romaji": "Namashirasudon",
      "zh_tw": "生しらす丼",
      "en": "Nama shirasu don (Fresh shirasu rice bowl)"
    },
    "prefecture": "kanagawa",
    "category": "kyodo",
    "summary": {
      "text": "Fresh raw shirasu (baby sardines) on vinegared rice (or white rice) is served on top of a bowl of rice. It is a well-known specialty of the Shonan area, including Chigasaki, Kamakura, and Enoshima.Shirasu are young sardines. Boiled shirasu is called \"kama-age shirasu\" and sun-dried shirasu is called \"shirasu-boshi.\" Nama-shirasu, as the name implies, is raw unprocessed shirasu.",
